{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>How long will you refuse to keep.</b> The sin of failing to keep was committed by all of you: you too, even though you did not go out with them to gather, caused them to go out — for you did not teach them the laws of Sabbath and their significance. You only said, 'Six days you shall gather it' and not seven days, and thereby they rebelled against your word; and you said, 'But on the seventh day, a Sabbath, there will be none in it' — yet they did not believe your word. But you did not teach them My commandments: that gathering the manna falls under the category of melakhah, so that the one who gathers is liable because of תּוֹלֵשׁ (uprooting), and that carrying it from domain to domain is likewise included among the melakhot." "<b>And My torot.</b> The nature of the Sabbath, its reason, its reward and its punishment — so that all who know them will take care to keep the Sabbath without doubt."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The addressee throughout is Moses, whom YHWH holds partly responsible for the people's Sabbath violation because he had not adequately instructed them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:54.839848329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}